think Standfast check: crux/REDS.md living rows 80, 83, 84, 85 all CLOSED or fixed-in-round with a witness on metal; only #75 rests as custody-gated errata. The line is clear to take new constructive work.
think Chose the crux-first, agent-doable rung the recent recommends named: a per-cluster facts/bounding-box join over the connected components just built -- the payoff of overlap_clusters. Where overlap_clusters answers WHO belongs to which cluster, this rung answers WHAT each cluster is: its union frame and its joined facts. Lindy-first (a scene-read primitive a Photos/marketplace surface reads for years), crux-first (the hardest-solvable move that opens the next scene reads).
think Read the modules it composes over: overlap_clusters.rye (Clustering, cluster_of, cluster_size), scene_graph.rye (SceneGraph carries the manifest and the relation matrix), scene_manifest.rye (ObjectEntry with area/box/holes, is_holed), selection_bounds.rye (the Box union pattern and box_contains_object over-claim read). Followed the family's local-builder selftest pattern and the native-contains witness template (REDS #85).
think Designed the DECISIVE crux one step past selection_bounds: there the frame over-claimed within one selection; here the cluster frame OVER-CLAIMS MEMBERSHIP ACROSS CLUSTERS. Two bracket-L's reaching apart (A box (1,1)-(6,6), B a ring box (4,4)-(9,9)) whose boxes overlap through the shared corner (4,4)-(6,6) connect into ONE cluster whose union frame spans (1,1)-(9,9); a lone block C (box (8,1)-(9,2)) sits in the top-right gap outside either member's box (x>6 clears A, y<4 clears B), so C is its own singleton -- yet the cluster frame wholly contains C. Containment of a box is never membership of a cluster; only cluster_of says who belongs. Second shape: object_relation proves A and B sit 2+ pixels APART, so the cluster's total area 31 (A 11 + ring 20) is far less than its frame's area 81 -- a group of FRAMES never of substance.
think Verified the scene geometry by hand before building: raster labeling numbers A=1 (first pixel (1,1)), C=2 ((8,1)), B=3 ((4,4)); every object 2+ pixels from every other (distinct 8-components) while A.box and B.box overlap; the ring is holed (area 20, one hole). The selftest asserts each box, area, and hole so the crux rests on measured placement, not memory.
obs GREEN on the FIRST full metal run -- no brace trap (no {...} in the print) and no compound asserts (kept each range check split preemptively from the prior laps' lessons). The ring gives the cluster a holed member and an unambiguous largest, so cluster_holed_count and largest_in_cluster prove real facts rather than a tie.
